{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773573179,"nonce":"5nTPU+9tOD2dOxSWpw3wFOL4dR8=","title":"Agent loops infinitely on orphan resume when task is too complex","message":"When the agent hits max_turns and the container exits with status 'working', the watcher detects it as orphaned and auto-resumes. If the task is too big, the agent hits max_turns again at the same checkpoint, dies again, and the watcher restarts it — creating an infinite loop.\n\nFix: track orphan_resumes count in state.json. After MAX_ORPHAN_RESUMES (3) restarts, suspend the session as 'suspended:too-complex' and post a comment asking to split the task.\n\nREQ-002, REQ-004","files":null}]}